[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. set up the one-level sub-frame of a floor and the two-free-joint sub-frame of a beam: the members, their stiffnesses (full K or ½K) and the fixed far ends;
2. run a moment distribution with the columns in the joints, and find the column moments and the moments at their far ends;
3. choose the load cases each sub-frame needs, and build the envelope of the beam moments, the shears and the column moments;
4. compare the continuous beam, the two-free-joint and the one-level sub-frames, and explain which moments each one overestimates or underestimates;
5. choose the values that go into the design of the beams and the columns.
